# walk_forward_all_candidates.csv is regenerated in full on every run of
# refresh-walk-forward-candidates.yml and is only ever persisted to git as
# the gzip-compressed walk_forward_all_candidates.csv.gz (see that workflow's
# "Commit refreshed candidates" step). The plain .csv is a local/CI working
# file only; keeping it untracked stops it from ever being re-added by
# `git add -u` or `git add -A` by accident.
walk_forward_all_candidates.csv

# train_data.csv is regenerated in full (not appended) on every run of
# daily-model-retrain.yml and refresh-walk-forward-candidates.yml. It is not
# persisted to git at all (not even gzip-compressed): both workflows upload
# it as a 30-day Actions artifact instead, since committing any version of
# it (plain or .gz) grows the repository forever. The plain .csv and any
# leftover .gz are local/CI working files only; keeping them untracked stops
# them from ever being re-added by `git add -u` or `git add -A` by accident.
train_data.csv
train_data.csv.gz
